==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|foreswear}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|forsweren|}}, from {{inh|en|ang|forswerian||to swear falsely}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|farswerian}}, {{cog|goh|farsweren}}, {{cog|de|verschwören}}. More at {{prefix|en|for|swear}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/fə(ɹ)ˈswɛə(ɹ)/|/fɔː(ɹ)ˈswɛə(ɹ)/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-forswear.wav ‎|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|forswears|forswearing|forswore|forsworn}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[renounce]] or [[deny]] [[something]], especially under [[oath]].
#: {{ux|en|We '''forswear''' allegiance and support for the Economic Freedom Fighters.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=Never to woo her more; but do '''forswear''' her.|author={{w|William Shakespeare}}|title={{w|The Taming of the Shrew}}|year=1592}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=Like Innocence, and as serenely bold / As Truth, how loudly He '''forswears''' thy Gold!.|author={{w|John Dryden}}, translating {{w|Juvenal}}|title=Satires|year=1726|url=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=2L0DAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA192&dq=dryden+forswears+thy+gold&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwixluKCxrfRAhVDbbwKHa-eCkYQ6AEIQzAH#v=onepage&q=dryden%20forswears%20thy%20gold&f=false}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=Either '''forswear''' fucking others or the affair is over.|author={{w|Philip Roth}}|title=Sabbath's Theater|year=1995|url=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=RqqYrLmrcbYC&pg=PA3&dq=forswear&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiQn-bmw7fRAhXCVbwKHVN3ADk4ChDoAQgvMAQ#v=onepage&q=forswear&f=false}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2008
|author={{w|Philip Roth}}
|title={{w|Indignation (novel)|Indignation}}
|section=
|passage= The sheer unimaginableness of coming into her mouth — of coming into anything other than the air or a tissue or a dirty sock — was an allurement too stupendous for a novice to '''forswear'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|or|reflexive}} To [[commit]] [[perjury]]; to [[break]] an [[oath]].

